WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.223
- But if you turn around and you look,

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.250
everything you see is new.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.370
That's 10 rows each with about 15 cars

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:12.390
It's probably 150, 175 cars.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.620
- [Host] It's what you'd expect to see

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.840
at a car dealership like Adam Lee's.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.300
But let's rewind eight months.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.760
- Look at this, I have not
walked out here in a while.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.283
This is, it's a lot of lot.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.800
- Last year, new car sales fell

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.900
to their lowest level in over a decade

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.800
as shoppers saw more asphalt
than cars on dealer lots.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.930
Now, fast forward to today, dealers

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.480
like Adam Lee finally
have more cars to sell

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.120
but rising interest rates
are making those cars

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.590
harder to afford.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:44.400
So the question is, will more
inventory equal more sales

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.400
or will shoppers hold
out for better prices?

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.220
Let's step back onto Lee's
Lot to see what's going on

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.880
with the car market right now
and if 2023 will be a boom

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.713
or bust year for the industry?

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.180
Here at Lee's Dodge
Chrysler Jeep Dealership

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.070
shoppers have options.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:05.400
- We have a great selection of
everything and it's unusual.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.020
I mean, just we haven't
had a good selection

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.410
of anything for three years.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:13.500
- [Host] JD Power Reports
inventory at dealerships climbed

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.870
over 1 million cars to start the year.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:18.210
It was around 800,000 last summer

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:21.060
but hovered around 3 million, pre-COVID.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.400
- Customers would like
to pull into a dealership

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.250
and have some choice, whether
it's color or equipment.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:29.070
I think they feel that
they're not being forced

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:32.070
into buying something that
maybe isn't quite perfect.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.920
- [Host] But visiting Lee's
Toyota Lot you wouldn't know

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.450
inventory is up.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.840
- We have about 10 or 12 new
cars on the lot, however,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.000
all but probably six of 'em are sold.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.490
- [Host] This imbalance
between Lee's two dealerships

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:47.430
doesn't surprise JD Powers, Tyson Jonney.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:50.076
- My word of 2023 is asymmetry.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:52.830
We will expect production to come back

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.330
but it's gonna be asymmetric.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.220
Some automakers will come back sooner

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.190
across the portfolio and even some models

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:01.770
within an automaker's
portfolio won't return

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:02.880
at the same time.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.160
- [Host] Take a look at
supply by brand in January.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.220
Cox Automotive shows Jeep
a brand Lee had a lot of

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.800
with 125 days of supply.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.500
Well, Toyota had less than 30 days.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.020
- It would be nice to see a
few more new cars sitting here.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.390
People would like to, we're selling cars

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.122
to people that are waiting six months

00:02:20.122 --> 00:02:22.530
and they've never even driven the car.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:24.960
So people like to at least try it out.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.090
- [Host] Still, like other
dealers, Lee is quick

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.600
to say he doesn't want his
pre-pandemic inventory back

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.050
and for now it seems
neither do the automakers.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.810
- We're closely monitoring
the dynamic macro-environment

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:39.900
as well as customer demand to
make sure we're appropriately

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.820
matching supply with demand.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.580
- [Host] A big reason for that pricing.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.070
There's a strong correlation
between vehicle pricing

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.210
and inventory.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:50.100
Roughly speaking, the
more cars on the lot,

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.680
the more the dealer might be
forced to consider discounts

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.280
or a manufacturer might offer
incentives to move vehicles.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.280
- It's not great for us and
it's not ideal for the consumer,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.300
if you buy a car today

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.190
and then two months from now
you see that car advertised

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.230
for $6,000 less than you just paid

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.091
it's better if maybe there
was a little moderation,

00:03:06.091 --> 00:03:10.650
start with a reasonable
price and just stick to that.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:13.260
- [Host] But even a quick look
in car windows will tell you

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:17.100
many vehicle prices aren't
exactly reasonable right now.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:20.553
- This is your random
average, inexpensive Jeep.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:23.183
It's not so bad.

00:03:23.183 --> 00:03:27.180
$39,000, it's still a lot, but the trucks

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.790
these trucks are 60, $70,000.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:33.120
So it's a challenge in
the industry as a whole.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.650
- [Host] The average cost of a new vehicle

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.440
was nearly $47,000 last month,

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.320
the second highest month
on record after December.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.750
But Joni says those
high transaction prices

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.100
aren't here to stay.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.850
Incentives are near record
lows now, but JD Power projects

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:50.400
they could hit 8% by year's end.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.820
- Nowadays what we can see
is a return to incentives

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:55.590
advertising in the marketing.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.600
So if you're looking for a full
size pickup and you see one

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.000
on TV, a commercial that last five seconds

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.230
you're gonna start to see a deal.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.090
- [Narrator] 2.99%
financing for five years

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.640
on all 2022 Silverado 1500 pickups.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.840
- [Host] But for many buyers,

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.060
it's the monthly payment they look at most

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.740
and rapidly rising interest rates

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:13.530
have made those payments more expensive.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:14.940
- Just pick a vehicle here.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.107
Any one of these, the
payments gonna go up,

00:04:17.107 --> 00:04:20.670
$80 a month with a five
point rate increase.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:24.390
So it hurts the consumer
and they get nothing for it.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:27.120
- [Host] Last year a lack of
cars kept interested buyers

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.170
out of the market.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:30.120
Now the worry is higher rates

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.236
or even a possible recession
will dampen demand.

00:04:33.236 --> 00:04:35.400
- When we're bringing on more production

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:39.300
and starting to return to
normalcy, we really concerned

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.510
that economic factors may
just knock the industry out

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:43.343
at the knees here

00:04:43.343 --> 00:04:45.510
and consumers will stay out of the market.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:48.000
- [Host] But after years
of empty dealerships

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.280
there's a lot of pent up demand.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:53.400
JD Power estimated two and
a half million shoppers

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.440
are still looking to buy a car.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.520
- This 2.5 million is mission
critical to the auto industry

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.280
in 2023 for helping it achieve the plan

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.200
which really is to see sales increase

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.750
by about a million units
this year from last year.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.760
- [Host] Vehicle sales are
expected to hit as many

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.760
as 15 million for the
year more than last year

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:14.610
though still below pre-pandemic levels.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.820
But to hit that number,
demand has to hold.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:20.640
And some dealers see warning signs.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.650
- If they keep raising rates

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:24.900
and the manufacturers don't respond,

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:28.860
sales are gonna decline
dramatically because people

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:32.460
they just, they can't spend
six, seven, $800 a month

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.650
for a new SUV or a truck.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.650
- [Host] But Domini says 2023
could actually be kind of

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:38.790
a sweet spot year

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:40.957
for the industry where
buyers have more choice

00:05:40.957 --> 00:05:42.960
but not so much selection

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.090
that the heavy discounting returns.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:48.810
- We had decades operating
at over 3 million vehicles

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:52.620
in inventory and we've had a
year operating under a million.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.330
We have never operated

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:57.240
at this quote sweet spot
where we want to get to.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.330
So if we get there, it
will be a new environment.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.640
- [Host] Achieving this
requires automakers to continue

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:03.473
to produce less

00:06:03.473 --> 00:06:06.450
than they had been something
Ford has said it would do.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:07.590
- We are not gonna go back

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:11.468
to the high inventories
that we had in the past.

00:06:11.468 --> 00:06:13.440
- The challenge is that,

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:16.440
there are at least 30
brands in the auto industry.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:19.410
So the ability to to
have discipline relies

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:22.950
on the other 29 competitors
also maintaining a form

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:23.790
of discipline.

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.260
- [Host] And it will also mean dealers

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.240
like Lee will have to continue to live

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:29.250
with at least some empty lot.

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:30.900
- We're still seeing empty lot.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:31.860
It's fine.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.780
It's a good place to push snow

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.046
and we don't need anymore
new cars right now.

00:06:36.046 --> 00:06:38.546
(soft music)

